      "message": "Just wondering if we have any plan to set `guest_state_protected` in the pKVM, and the potential usage in the pKVM? Now pKVM uses `is_guest_vcpu_accessible()` to check if a hypercall is allowed or not, and some hypercalls will not be allowed once the vcpu starts running by checking `kvm_vcpu_has_run(vcpu)`. So seems this behavior in the pKVM is similar to `guest_state_protected`, which is set after return from the first vcpu_run hypercall.",
